## What changed

- independently audited and froze the completed 10-cell minimal paired benchmark;
- rebuilt corrected runtime, PAR-2, numerical-reconciliation, table, and figure artifacts from immutable run records;
- audited all 20 Final Holdout baseline anchors and the paired rho 0 to 0.01 transition;
- added solver-free deterministic reporting and archive regression tests.

## Scientific scope

No optimization result, model, Farkas certificate, Hybrid branching rule, source ZIP, `src/benders.py`, or `src/scenarios.py` is changed. The reports retain all preregistered cells and use PAR-2 for uncertified reference runs.

## Validation

- benchmark: 10/10 complete, 3/10 reference certified, 7/10 time-limit uncertified;
- post-evaluation: 222/222 chunk SHAs, 5,493 scenarios, 60,426/60,426 accepted evidence;
- Final Holdout: existing 120-run strict audit passed; all 20 anchor gaps are below 1e-4;
- two independent report builds are byte-identical;
- new targeted tests: 4 passed;
- historical pre-run static audit now reports its expected output-directory-nonexistent condition as false because the benchmark has completed; no historical gate was weakened.
